- # `↯/s.100.4` — `EmailAddress.Error`
+ # `↯/s.100.4` — `EmailAddress.Error`

- Raised when a value cannot be parsed as a valid email address.
+ Lançado quando um valor não pode ser analisado como um endereço de e-mail válido.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Urticose validates email addresses against the syntax rules in
- RFC 5321 / 5322 (with practical relaxations). The message is `the
+ O Urticose valida endereços de e-mail contra as regras de sintaxe das RFC 5321 / 5322 (com
+ flexibilizações práticas). A mensagem é `the

- email address is not valid because $reason`.
+ email address is not valid because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.100.4.1`  `Empty`  The value is empty.  `[↯/s.100.4.1] the email address is not valid because it is empty`  Provide a non-empty address.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.2`  `InvalidDomain`  The domain part is neither a valid hostname nor a valid IP literal.  `[↯/s.100.4.2] the email address is not valid because the domain is not a valid hostname: the character _ is not allowed in a hostname`  Correct the domain syntax; consult the inner `HostnameError`/`IpAddress.Error` variant for specifics.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.3`  `LongLocalPart`  The local part exceeds 64 characters.  `[↯/s.100.4.3] the email address is not valid because the local part is more than 64 characters long`  Shorten the local part to at most 64 characters.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.4`  `TerminalPeriod`  The local part ends in a period.  `[↯/s.100.4.4] the email address is not valid because the local part ends in a period, which is not allowed`  Remove the trailing period.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.5`  `SuccessivePeriods`  The local part contains two adjacent periods.  `[↯/s.100.4.5] the email address is not valid because the local part contains two adjacent periods`  Remove one of the periods, or quote the local part if successive periods are required.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.6`  `InitialPeriod`  The local part starts with a period.  `[↯/s.100.4.6] the email address is not valid because the local part starts with a period, which is not allowed`  Remove the leading period.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.7`  `UnescapedQuote`  A double-quote in the local part was not escaped.  `[↯/s.100.4.7] the email address is not valid because the local part contains a quote character which is not escaped`  Either escape the quote with a backslash or use a properly quoted local part.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.8`  `UnclosedQuote`  The quoted local part has no closing quote.  `[↯/s.100.4.8] the email address is not valid because the quoted local part has no closing quote`  Add the missing `"`.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.9`  `MissingDomain`  The address has no domain part.  `[↯/s.100.4.9] the email address is not valid because the domain is missing`  Append `@` followed by the domain.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.10`  `MissingAtSymbol`  The address contains no `@`.  `[↯/s.100.4.10] the email address is not valid because the at-symbol is missing`  Insert `@` between the local part and the domain.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.11`  `UnclosedIpAddress`  The domain begins with `[` but does not end with `]`.  `[↯/s.100.4.11] the email address is not valid because the domain begins with [ but does not end with ]`  Close the IP-literal with `]`.
- row  `↯/s.100.4.12`  `InvalidChar`  The local part contains a character that is not allowed.  `[↯/s.100.4.12] the email address is not valid because the local part contains the character > which is not allowed`  Remove the offending character or quote the local part to permit it.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensagem
+ column  Resolução
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.1`  `Empty`  O valor está vazio.  `[↯/s.100.4.1] the email address is not valid because it is empty`  Forneça um endereço não vazio.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.2`  `InvalidDomain`  A parte do domínio não é nem um hostname válido nem um literal de IP válido.  `[↯/s.100.4.2] the email address is not valid because the domain is not a valid hostname: the character _ is not allowed in a hostname`  Corrija a sintaxe do domínio; consulte a variante interna de `HostnameError`/`IpAddress.Error` para os detalhes.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.3`  `LongLocalPart`  A parte local excede 64 caracteres.  `[↯/s.100.4.3] the email address is not valid because the local part is more than 64 characters long`  Encurte a parte local para no máximo 64 caracteres.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.4`  `TerminalPeriod`  A parte local termina com um ponto.  `[↯/s.100.4.4] the email address is not valid because the local part ends in a period, which is not allowed`  Remova o ponto final.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.5`  `SuccessivePeriods`  A parte local contém dois pontos adjacentes.  `[↯/s.100.4.5] the email address is not valid because the local part contains two adjacent periods`  Remova um dos pontos, ou ponha a parte local entre aspas se pontos sucessivos forem necessários.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.6`  `InitialPeriod`  A parte local começa com um ponto.  `[↯/s.100.4.6] the email address is not valid because the local part starts with a period, which is not allowed`  Remova o ponto inicial.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.7`  `UnescapedQuote`  Uma aspa dupla na parte local não foi escapada.  `[↯/s.100.4.7] the email address is not valid because the local part contains a quote character which is not escaped`  Escape a aspa com uma barra invertida ou use uma parte local corretamente posta entre aspas.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.8`  `UnclosedQuote`  A parte local entre aspas não tem aspa de fechamento.  `[↯/s.100.4.8] the email address is not valid because the quoted local part has no closing quote`  Acrescente o `"` que falta.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.9`  `MissingDomain`  O endereço não tem parte do domínio.  `[↯/s.100.4.9] the email address is not valid because the domain is missing`  Acrescente `@` seguido do domínio.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.10`  `MissingAtSymbol`  O endereço não contém `@`.  `[↯/s.100.4.10] the email address is not valid because the at-symbol is missing`  Insira `@` entre a parte local e o domínio.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.11`  `UnclosedIpAddress`  O domínio começa com `[` mas não termina com `]`.  `[↯/s.100.4.11] the email address is not valid because the domain begins with [ but does not end with ]`  Feche o literal de IP com `]`.
+ row  `↯/s.100.4.12`  `InvalidChar`  A parte local contém um caractere que não é permitido.  `[↯/s.100.4.12] the email address is not valid because the local part contains the character > which is not allowed`  Remova o caractere culpado ou ponha a parte local entre aspas para permiti-lo.

